// Configuration `monochromatic-lint` reads when the package wraps a passage
// (`semantic-wrap-binary.ts` names it with `--config`). It selects the one
// rule that puts line breaks back after a break-point character.
//
// The severity is "warn" on purpose. With "error" the program exits with
// status 1 whenever a finding survives its fix passes, even though the wrapped
// text is on standard output; the in-process wrap this replaced returned that
// text and ignored what survived, and a wrap that stopped a paid run over a
// cosmetic leftover would be worse than the leftover. A run that cannot be
// trusted to be complete still exits with status 2, which the package refuses.
[
  {
    "files": ["**/*.md"],
    "rules": {
      "markdown/semantic-line-breaks": { "severity": "warn" }
    }
  }
]
